H cases and cannot tell them apart.","The shipped _seatbelt_works probe (scripts/mutation_sandbox.py:131-135) does NOT key on exit status — it requires the _PROBE_MARKER on stdout precisely because 'absence alone is also what a failed launch looks like' (probe docstring lines 96-100). The enforcement tests should inherit that same discrimination, not a weaker exit-code check.","The plan's qualifier 'that only an executed-and-denied child produces' is the correct constraint, but the 'exit code' example read literally does not meet it — a launch failure also yields non-zero."],"finding":"One of the plan's own offered liveness forms — 'an asserted exit code' — does not by itself distinguish an executed-and-denied child from a child that never launched, which is the exact ambiguity the plan exists to remove.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4471d8a5de55d6be","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, first bullet: 'e.g. a sentinel written to an ALLOWED path in the same command, or an asserted exit code / stderr signature that only an executed-and-denied child produces'","norm_id":"nf631bc21a46d1f25","priority":0.75,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer reads the AC and satisfies liveness with `assert proc.returncode != 0`; sandbox-exec later regresses to a launch failure; the test stays green because a launch failure is also non-zero — reintroducing the false pass the plan set out to kill."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Replace 'an asserted exit code / stderr signature' with 'a stdout sentinel emitted (to an allowed path or stdout) BEFORE the denied action, or a stderr signature that a launch failure cannot produce — a bare non-zero exit code does NOT qualify, since a failed launch is also non-zero'. Mirror the shipped _seatbelt_works marker-plus-absence pattern (mutation_sandbox.py:131-135).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":